<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  the soft light behind the drawing at the top of the About screen.

  **it is what makes that screen a page rather than the first card of a list**, and it is the only
  ornament on it: a portrait dropped onto a flat surface floats, and a shape drawn behind it with an
  edge would be a second object competing with it. a radius that fades to nothing reads as light rather
  than as a thing.

  it is solid white and the layout tints it, which is `bg_badge.xml`'s rule and is here for the same
  reason: a shape's own colour cannot be a theme attribute on every API this app supports, where
  `android:backgroundTint` on the view can. the tint replaces the colour and keeps the alpha, so a
  white-to-transparent ramp becomes an accent-to-transparent one in whichever palette is on.

  **the middle stop is what shapes it.** two stops give a linear falloff, which has a visible disc in
  it; a third at just over a third of the alpha pulls the ramp in and leaves no edge anywhere. the view
  carries the overall strength as `android:alpha`, so the same drawable is a whisper under a near-white
  accent and a glow under a violet one.
-->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="oval">
    <gradient
        android:type="radial"
        android:gradientRadius="50%"
        android:startColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:centerColor="#59FFFFFF"
        android:endColor="#00FFFFFF" />
</shape>
